    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 11,
        "sourceEnd": 282,
        "text": "Good evening, everyone. I'm Maya Chen, chair of the Westbrook District school board. Tonight we discuss the new enrollment zones for Northside High and Riverbend High. Before we start, I want to say clearly: no final vote happens tonight. We are only collecting comments.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "476dd1d2e48b24e38031efed90a52b391e2b1ffbd048e13f617882dcaacfae7c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel ortiz",
        "speaker": "Daniel Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 298,
        "sourceEnd": 488,
        "text": "Thank you, Chair Chen. I'm Daniel Ortiz, parent of a seventh-grader. My main worry is busing. If Northside takes students from the east side, how long will the ride be? Forty minutes? Fifty?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a64205d374bb0ff5a46a79b6fc116e16ff6484d95e9eae2524b38ea34dbb91e6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 501,
        "sourceEnd": 638,
        "text": "The transport office estimates thirty-five to forty-five minutes for the farthest streets. Not fifty. I checked that number this morning.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "13b08718a2e88eda1bb1606e2b6e0d8342857cf66bcd86b2b909e2bf6c641481",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel ortiz",
        "speaker": "Daniel Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 654,
        "sourceEnd": 733,
        "text": "All right, thirty-five to forty-five. That is still long for a twelve-year-old.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "7a677fc35dc321a0a350eca253b0ad45dfe640f990136f9b761cf434917048cc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya nair",
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "sourceStart": 747,
        "sourceEnd": 1045,
        "text": "I'm Priya Nair, and I teach science at Riverbend. I want to correct something I heard in the hallway. People say Riverbend has fewer lab spaces than Northside. That is not true. Riverbend has four labs; Northside has three. The real problem is not the number of labs. It is that our labs are older.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "451e469f67d94df64083f79a7aa5d12f103ece8d72ba70f3cf94aed7ea083ef8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1058,
        "sourceEnd": 1122,
        "text": "Thank you for the correction. So the issue is age, not quantity.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "23fbc78f9d279d620b8a4500f96b21247b4344637b3ef2d6f6c849489739cdb2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya nair",
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "sourceStart": 1136,
        "sourceEnd": 1276,
        "text": "Exactly. And one more point: not every Riverbend student lives far away. About sixty percent walk or cycle. Only a minority depend on buses.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "cc5a1293d40fcbdde739f1899881853c6654b0022b708d5d0cebc810db9375ab",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom becker",
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "sourceStart": 1290,
        "sourceEnd": 1608,
        "text": "I'm Tom Becker, from the parent council. I have a question about capacity. Northside can hold nine hundred students. Riverbend can hold seven hundred and fifty. Right now Northside has eight hundred and ten, and Riverbend has seven hundred and ninety. So Riverbend is already over its limit, and Northside is not full.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "102c439e64e491911eedfd7e00cc5d8056da4de9a9eb2760854a33db4663661e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1621,
        "sourceEnd": 1720,
        "text": "That matches our data. Riverbend is forty students over capacity. Northside has ninety empty seats.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "e2dd1c34024983ffb0651a534abd635028be123335925a0d15ab16071eb9b5dc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom becker",
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "sourceStart": 1734,
        "sourceEnd": 1802,
        "text": "Then why move more students to Riverbend? That makes no sense to me.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "2fff4740955771aee9c90592d48a1de8c491766dcb8ee7312c3b7bdbe6cdee51",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1815,
        "sourceEnd": 1969,
        "text": "The proposal does not move students to Riverbend. It moves a small group from the crowded east side to Northside. I think you have the direction reversed.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "1abb0b9909915662708ee5ed4d409dfb3459ba5e6373795bc00148882845ed15",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom becker",
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "sourceStart": 1983,
        "sourceEnd": 2060,
        "text": "Oh — I did have it reversed. Sorry. So the east-side group goes to Northside.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "ba72161ea111c0901e9720cb524e74d30c3901e558bcef468c9733e86e427fc3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2073,
        "sourceEnd": 2168,
        "text": "Yes. About one hundred and twenty students would move. Not two hundred. One hundred and twenty.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "a975ba432e063eab3897023dee56c8c822022eb51edb30f1f1fb8e81782b75bc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel ortiz",
        "speaker": "Daniel Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 2184,
        "sourceEnd": 2279,
        "text": "Can I ask about timing? My daughter starts high school next year. Will the change apply to her?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "e76cb0df2e897ce46ea563e7c06d43a2a543ef2f44488302938a60b0665e1c90",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2292,
        "sourceEnd": 2490,
        "text": "The new zones would begin in September of next year. Students already in grade ten or eleven would not be forced to move. Only incoming grade nine students and new arrivals would follow the new map.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "190e4803258bec3ec052721dd59c1bfa3be5b301c3e4f5137e3a454b986a7d7d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya nair",
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "sourceStart": 2504,
        "sourceEnd": 2564,
        "text": "That is an important detail. So current older students stay.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3dd500e2f06c1e23a5ad267da8c20fcb4a837c50550d857c1e7f3e1ee95a1177",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2577,
        "sourceEnd": 2672,
        "text": "Correct. They stay if they choose to stay. Nobody is removed from a school they already attend.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "809e5c6c58b89d2018b3f50c500ca8c16cf5d239f1bc06f6fcfd33209504d6ae",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom becker",
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "sourceStart": 2686,
        "sourceEnd": 2759,
        "text": "What about the budget? I read that the change saves money. Is that right?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "2a17063a88549a9321f4b917b8910ecc315e3c2a333373220cb4b9da0d9ed8d9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2772,
        "sourceEnd": 2961,
        "text": "Partly. The district expects to save on bus fuel, but it will spend more on extra classrooms at Northside. The savings are smaller than the new costs. So the plan is not mainly about money.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "8d6e2c5e4efde2bd5fff5e315df6d04edac66b455ce84bc3c1362076cc8994a0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel ortiz",
        "speaker": "Daniel Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 2977,
        "sourceEnd": 3006,
        "text": "Then what is it mainly about?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "320fba0bc489cdca7a1f05e731305df9bfaacd39a26323d3a3ee6f9be16c5793",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 3019,
        "sourceEnd": 3223,
        "text": "Fair access. East-side students currently travel farther to reach a school with fewer science labs. Northside has more lab space and shorter trips for those families. The aim is to reduce that inequality.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "87ab613b02297dc529c7c553b9ffbe083c0e57e2a627da99bcd3675fe68285ba",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya nair",
        "speaker": "Priya Nair",
        "sourceStart": 3237,
        "sourceEnd": 3355,
        "text": "I support the aim, but I want a promise. If Northside gets more students, it needs more teachers, not just more rooms.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "7920a0856ceceddab673f213a207dcbe570efe15e245487484a40297d053298a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 3368,
        "sourceEnd": 3469,
        "text": "That is a fair request. I will add it to the minutes: teacher numbers must grow with student numbers.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "bc9d05e6546968eca5932d2c6fa9d897c425c5a7c475fec32054a7a0acee4b3a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "tom becker",
        "speaker": "Tom Becker",
        "sourceStart": 3483,
        "sourceEnd": 3531,
        "text": "One last thing. When is the next public meeting?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "e3bec5d4639ea60e7d3e8539867b64923b9e434169e731609282e52e7fba9503",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 3544,
        "sourceEnd": 3761,
        "text": "The next meeting is on the fourteenth of March, at seven in the evening, in the Northside library. Not the Riverbend library — Northside. Please check the district website before you come, because the room may change.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "92c71d0465bf7d4c39af8fb13d3c0c6008e31334d6846aecac5a62665e17a60b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel ortiz",
        "speaker": "Daniel Ortiz",
        "sourceStart": 3777,
        "sourceEnd": 3827,
        "text": "Thank you. That was clearer than the last meeting.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "4c047a35b128dca7922f684a4d3f188032b1b2c08c5e1f08190970525490c4e3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya chen",
        "speaker": "Maya Chen",
        "sourceStart": 3840,
        "sourceEnd": 3899,
        "text": "Thank you all. Remember: comments tonight, no vote tonight.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "e4885e3720d77a06fcd650f6dd633a137b97cd71c53aad63f5c31dc6509f3a5b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
